    "created_at": "2017-07-01T00:10:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-01T00:10:15Z",
    "body": "Thought about this for another second. This can potentially lead to webcompat issue in the future, actually.\r\n\r\nI mean, if poping up dialog leads to exiting fullscreen in Chrome, could websites rely on that in the future in some case that they should really use `exitFullscreen`? e.g., if a website enters fullscreen, and pop up a dialog, and the developer tests it on Chrome and finds it exits fullscreen, then they may assume it would just exit fullscreen everywhere. In that case, other browsers would be left in fullscreen while the page thinks it has exited.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/comments/312397283/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
